Recently named one of Lhasa's ten most inspiring people, Nima Wando's story reflects the hope
尼玛旺多最近被评为拉萨十大励志人物之一，他的故事反映了

18
00:02:13,719 --> 00:02:19,960
and progress in the region experienced by people from different communities today.
当今来自不同社区的人们在该地区所感受到的希望与进步。

19
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,960
Here's our conversation.
以下是我们的对话。

20
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,960
Nima Wando means the power of sun.
尼玛旺多意为太阳的力量。

21
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,960
I'm blind and I'm totally blind.
我是盲人，而且是全盲。

22
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,960
I cannot see anything.
我什么都看不见。

23
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:37,800
And I am from East Tibet from Ganze and I have a twin sister and my look, I think no
我来自西藏东部的甘孜，我有个双胞胎姐妹，至于我的长相，我觉得

24
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,960
need to explain so many girls things that I'm so handsome.
没必要多解释了，大家都说我长得挺帅的。

25
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,960
I think so too.
我也这么觉得。

26
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,460
Okay, good.
好的，不错。

27
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:48,960
Yeah, this is me Nima Wando and I also have my book.
是的，这就是我，尼玛旺多，我还带着我的书。

28
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,960
I love climbing.
我喜欢登山。

29
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:57,960
I love doing like jogging or like going for marathons and so on.
我也喜欢慢跑或者参加马拉松之类的活动。

30
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:01,960
So you became blind at a very young age, I understand.
我听说你很小就失明了。

31
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,460
That's right.
没错。

32
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:08,960
Yeah, actually when I was three months old I became blind and when I do talk some people
是的，其实我三个月大的时候就失明了，当我谈论这件事时，有些人

33
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:12,960
ask me said, when you were born three months, can you remember anything?
会问我，说你出生三个月的时候，你能记得什么吗？

34
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:14,460
And I asked the same question.
我也问了同样的问题。

35
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:16,960
I said, like when you were three months old, can you remember anything?
我说，就像你三个月大的时候，你能记得什么吗？

36
00:04:16,959 --> 00:04:18,959
They said, no, no, I didn't remember anything.
他们说，不，不，我什么都不记得。

37
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:22,959
So it's sent for me that I haven't seen anything.
所以对我来说，我并没有看到过任何东西。

38
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:26,959
But I want to make it clear here if I may.
但我想在这里澄清一下，如果我可以的话。

39
00:04:26,959 --> 00:04:30,959
I want to say is that we are not living in the dark.
我想说的是，我们并不是生活在黑暗中。

40
00:04:30,959 --> 00:04:33,959
How do you perceive the environment we're in now?
你如何感知我们现在所处的环境？

41
00:04:33,959 --> 00:04:35,959
I can feel the atmosphere here.
我能感受到这里的气氛。

42
00:04:35,959 --> 00:04:39,959
For us, we have our own way of seeing things.
对我们来说，我们有自己的看待事物的方式。

43
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:44,959
For example, I can smell a beautiful like, you know, tasty food.
例如，我能闻到一种美丽的，你知道的，美味的食物。

44
00:04:45,959 --> 00:04:48,959
I feel like here is like 40 square meters.
我感觉这里大约有40平方米。

45
00:04:48,959 --> 00:04:50,959
I don't know right or wrong.
我不知道对不对。

46
00:04:50,959 --> 00:04:52,959
And there are all kinds of sounds, right?
而且这里有各种各样的声音，对吧？

47
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,459
You pick up sounds.
你会捕捉到声音。

48
00:04:53,959 --> 00:04:55,459
How do you perceive this world?
你是如何感知这个世界的？

49
00:04:54,959 --> 00:04:59,959
Through sounds, through language, and also I think we have imagination.
通过声音，通过语言，而且我认为我们还有想象力。

50
00:04:59,959 --> 00:05:04,959
What I'm trying to say here is that we are living in our own world.
我想说的是，我们生活在自己的世界里。

51
00:05:04,959 --> 00:05:11,959
When you say beautiful girl, I also have my girl in my head.
当你说漂亮女孩时，我脑海里也有我的女孩。

52
00:05:11,959 --> 00:05:14,959
I don't know it's right or wrong, but I feel she's beautiful, right?
我不知道这是否正确，但我觉得她很美，对吧？

53
00:05:14,959 --> 00:05:22,959
The way how she talks, I can see her heart more than other people can see.
她说话的方式，让我比其他人更能看到她的内心。

54
00:05:22,959 --> 00:05:24,459
Inner beauty.
内在美。

55
00:05:23,959 --> 00:05:25,959
Yes, exactly. Inner beauty.
是的，没错。内在美。

56
00:05:25,959 --> 00:05:30,959
I think that's more important than the outside beauty, than inner beauty is something more important.
我认为这比外在美更重要，内在美是更重要的东西。

57
00:05:30,959 --> 00:05:35,959
I see. So you're kind of perceiving with your brain, with your mind and your heart.
我明白了。所以你是在用大脑、心灵和心去感知。

58
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:37,459
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

59
00:05:36,959 --> 00:05:42,959
That's very interesting because you have written a book actually called I don't want to be called Santhina Guangming.
这很有趣，因为你实际上写了一本书，叫《我不想被叫做光明》。

60
00:05:42,959 --> 00:05:47,959
And you translate that into no need to see three days.
你把它翻译成《无需看见三天》。

61
00:05:47,959 --> 00:05:52,959
Because that's kind of a nod or a head shake.
因为那有点像点头或摇头。

62
00:05:52,959 --> 00:05:54,459
You're shaking your head.
你在摇头。

63
00:05:53,959 --> 00:05:58,959
You say no to Helen Keller who said three days to see.
你对海伦·凯勒说‘不’，她说过如果有三天能看见。

64
00:05:58,959 --> 00:06:01,959
You say we don't need three days to see.
你说我们不需要三天来看见。

65
00:06:01,959 --> 00:06:03,459
What do you mean by that?
你这是什么意思？

66
00:06:02,959 --> 00:06:06,959
Actually some people think that I'm against for Helen Keller.
实际上有些人认为我是反对海伦·凯勒的。

67
00:06:06,959 --> 00:06:11,959
Actually I'm not against him because when I came to the world, she already gone.
其实我并不是反对她，因为当我来到这个世界时，她已经不在了。

68
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:15,959
But what I'm trying to say here is that I'm trying to put my view.
但我想在这里表达的是，我在陈述我的观点。

69
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:20,959
I am 36 years old and I haven't seen anything yet.
我今年36岁，却什么都看不见。

70
00:06:20,959 --> 00:06:25,959
If I have three days to see, I have so many people to see.
如果我有三天能看见，我有太多的人想见。

71
00:06:25,959 --> 00:06:27,959
I have so many my friends.
我有太多的朋友。

72
00:06:27,959 --> 00:06:29,959
I have so many important people.
我有太多重要的人。

73
00:06:29,959 --> 00:06:34,959
So if I only have three days to see those people, I believe this is not enough.
所以如果我只用三天时间去见那些人，我相信这是不够的。

74
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:39,959
And also the scary thing is after three days, I will be blind again.
而且可怕的事情是，三天之后，我又会重新陷入黑暗。

75
00:06:39,959 --> 00:06:41,959
So I feel like three days is nothing.
所以我觉得三天根本不算什么。

76
00:06:41,959 --> 00:06:49,959
I can accept who am I now and the way how I live is I feel like I'm pretty happy.
我能接受现在的自己，以及我生活方式，我觉得我很幸福。

77
00:06:49,959 --> 00:06:51,459
So I can accept who am I.
所以我能接受现在的自己。

78
00:06:50,959 --> 00:06:55,959
That's why I proudly say I don't need to see three days.
这就是为什么我自豪地说，我不需要看三天。

79
00:06:55,959 --> 00:07:00,959
Tell me then because you had a really hard childhood.
告诉我，因为你童年非常艰难。

80
00:07:00,959 --> 00:07:02,459
Really hard, right?
真的很难，对吗？

81
00:07:01,959 --> 00:07:05,959
You at the age of three months, you lost your eyesight.
你三个月大的时候，失去了视力。

82
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:07,459
Your father left you.
你的父亲离开了你。

83
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:08,459
Your mother later left you.
你的母亲后来也离开了你。

84
00:07:07,959 --> 00:07:10,959
You grew up in hardship, absolute hardship.
你在苦难中长大，绝对的苦难。

85
00:07:10,959 --> 00:07:14,959
But it seems that all of that did not make you bitter.
但似乎这一切并没有让你变得愤世嫉俗。

86
00:07:14,959 --> 00:07:20,959
Did not instead you are laughing, you're very optimistic and you're inspiring others.
相反，你在笑，你非常乐观，并且激励着他人。

87
00:07:20,959 --> 00:07:24,959
How come where do you get that strength and motivation?
这是怎么回事？你从何处获得这种力量和动力？

88
00:07:24,959 --> 00:07:28,959
I think a lot of success people went through a hard time.
我认为很多成功人士都经历过艰难时期。

89
00:07:28,959 --> 00:07:30,959
They had hard times.
他们经历过艰难时期。

90
00:07:30,959 --> 00:07:37,959
Also same for me, if I had a good childhood, I think I'm not the today's Nimon.
对我来说也一样，如果我有一个幸福的童年，我想我就不会成为今天的Nimon。

91
00:07:37,959 --> 00:07:40,959
When was the turning point?
转折点是什么时候？

92
00:07:40,959 --> 00:07:43,959
I think it depends.
我觉得要看情况。

93
00:07:43,959 --> 00:07:45,959
You have some points.
你有些观点。

94
00:07:45,959 --> 00:07:49,959
For example, when you are a kid, you also have some point, right?
比如，当你还是个孩子的时候，你也有自己的看法，对吧？

95
00:07:49,959 --> 00:07:54,959
For example, when I was a kid, so many people say like Shara or like blind fool.
比如，我小时候，很多人叫我“瞎子”或者“盲痴”。

96
00:07:54,959 --> 00:07:56,959
Shara means blind fool.
“Shara”的意思就是盲痴。

97
00:07:56,959 --> 00:08:00,959
When I say I want to see house racing, they say you are blind.
当我说我想看赛车比赛时，他们说我是瞎子。

98
00:08:00,959 --> 00:08:04,959
When I say I want to see the music concert, they say you are blind.
当我说我想看音乐会时，他们说我是瞎子。

99
00:08:04,959 --> 00:08:09,959
At that time I was very sad, but later in life, those helped me.
那时候我很伤心，但后来在生活中，这些经历帮助了我。

100
00:08:09,959 --> 00:08:11,959
I can accept who am I.
我能接受真实的自己。

101
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:13,959
You're doing a lot of TED Talks.
你做了很多TED演讲。

102
00:08:13,959 --> 00:08:15,959
Yes, I did.
是的，我做了。

103
00:08:15,959 --> 00:08:19,959
You do a lot of TED Talks, you inspire other people.
你做了很多TED演讲，你激励了其他人。

104
00:08:19,959 --> 00:08:21,959
You go mountain climbing.
你去登山。

105
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:24,959
And you do talk shows.
你还参加脱口秀节目。

106
00:08:24,959 --> 00:08:26,959
What are you trying to do?
你想做什么？

107
00:08:26,959 --> 00:08:29,959
What is the goal that you are trying to achieve?
你试图达成的目标是什么？

108
00:08:29,959 --> 00:08:34,960
What I am trying to do is I think I want to be helpful for this society.
我想做的，是希望能为这个社会提供帮助。

109
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:44,960
I want to share my experience that I hope many people will not face the problems that I have faced.
我想分享我的经历，希望许多人不会像我一样面临那些问题。

110
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:52,960
I also am willing to share my happy times with them and I also can hope that they will also be happier.
我也愿意与他们分享我的快乐时光，并希望他们也能更快乐。

111
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:54,960
This is one reason.
这是其中一个原因。

112
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:57,960
The second reason is I want to be a blind ambassador.
第二个原因是我想成为一名盲人大使。

113
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:05,960
I can say that what is blind and where we need help, where we no need help.
我可以说明什么是盲人，以及我们在哪里需要帮助，哪里不需要帮助。

114
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:08,960
Even we are blind, we can do a lot.
即使我们是盲人，我们也能做很多事情。

115
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:11,960
I think that people can do more than this.
我认为人们能做到的比这更多。

116
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:14,960
This is my message that I am trying to give.
这就是我想传达的信息。

117
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:25,960
What is the perception of people when you are talking to people here in Lhasa, in Shizang, somewhere else in China or even in other parts of the world?
当你在拉萨、西藏、中国其他地方甚至世界其他地方与人交谈时，人们对你的看法是什么？

118
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,960
Can people relate to you?
人们能与你产生共鸣吗？

119
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:33,960
I think 90% of people like my talk because I don't talk big things.
我认为90%的人喜欢我的演讲，因为我不谈宏大的事情。

120
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:39,960
I try to talk in daily life what we do, what I can do and also doing this in action.
我试着谈论日常生活中我们做什么，我能做什么，并且付诸行动。

121
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:42,960
For example, I say getting up early in the morning is important.
比如，我说早起很重要。

122
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:45,960
I do get up in the morning, I do go jogging.
我确实会早起，也确实会去慢跑。

123
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,960
They think that Nimon is doing what he is saying.
他们认为尼蒙（Nimon）是言行一致的。

124
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:50,460
This is number one.
这是第一点。

125
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:57,960
The second thing is I think my talk giving them hope, say that this blind person can do this, I could do this.
第二点是，我认为我的演讲给了他们希望，让他们觉得既然这位盲人能做到，我也能做到。

126
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:04,960
So let's example, one student his age is a little bit older than his classmates.
举个例子，有一个学生，他的年龄比同班同学稍大一些。

127
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:08,960
He is thinking about quitting when he went to the high school.
当他上高中时，他正考虑退学。

128
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:19,960
But after listening to my talk he said he found hope and he did manage to go to continually to high school and university.
但在听了我的演讲后，他说他找到了希望，并且确实坚持读完了高中和大学。

129
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:24,960
This makes me happy and also gives me hope for myself.
这让我感到高兴，也给了我自己的希望。

130
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:28,960
Where you go around the world and give talks? Where have you been?
你在全世界哪些地方做过演讲？你去过哪里？

131
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:36,960
I have been to the USA, Germany and I studied in England, Korea, Japan and so on.
我去过美国、德国，还在英国、韩国、日本等地学习过。

132
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:43,960
When you talk about your home, when you talk about what you do, what is the reaction of people?
当你谈到你的家乡，谈到你的工作时，人们的反应是什么？

133
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:48,960
I think number one is when I say I am from Shizan, they think wow, this is number one.
我认为第一点是，当我说我来自石嘴山（Shizan）时，他们觉得哇，这是第一点。

134
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:55,960
The second thing is that they think I am an easy going person and friendly and happy person.
第二点是，他们认为我是一个随和、友好且快乐的人。

135
00:10:55,960 --> 00:11:00,960
Because so many people think that blind people are not happy people or whatever.
因为很多人认为盲人是不快乐的，或者诸如此类。

136
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:05,960
But when they see us they feel like wow, my God, it changes their mindset.
但当我们出现在他们面前时，他们会惊叹：天哪，这改变了他们的观念。

137
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,960
This is what I hope as well.
这也是我所希望的。

138
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:18,960
I am just happy person and I try to give a good feeling or give try to share my energy with you guys.
我只是一个快乐的人，我试着传递美好的感觉，或者试着与你们分享我的能量。

139
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,960
I can certainly feel that.
我确实能感受到这一点。

140
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:29,960
Going forward, is it easy for other children with disabilities?
展望未来，对于其他残疾儿童来说，这容易吗？

141
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:38,960
Is it easy for them to fulfill their dreams, to go about and do the things that you do if they want to?
如果他们愿意，实现梦想、像您一样四处奔波并做您所做的那些事，对他们来说容易吗？

142
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:41,960
I think it is not about blindness or sighted people, whatever.
我认为这与盲人或明眼人无关，无论是什么身份。

143
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:47,960
I think it is same for everybody. If you are willing to work for your dreams, I think you can achieve your dreams.
我认为对每个人都是一样的。如果你愿意为你的梦想努力，我认为你就能实现你的梦想。

144
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:53,960
But if you are not willing to give up whatever you do for your dreams, I think it is same for everybody.
但如果你不愿意为了梦想而放弃你所做的一切，我认为对每个人都是一样的。

145
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:58,960
So those people are blind or whatever, whoever wants to achieve their dreams, I think they need to work hard.
所以，无论是盲人还是其他人，任何想要实现梦想的人，我认为都需要努力工作。

146
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:04,960
Because as you said, here I can say I went to the Harvard for talk, I went to TED talk.
因为正如你所说，在这里我可以讲，我去哈佛做过演讲，我去TED做过演讲。

147
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:07,960
So many people think it is easy, just few words.
很多人觉得这很容易，只是寥寥数语。

148
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:12,960
But I worked for a long time, I faced so many problems, I had so many challenges.
但我努力了很久，我面对了无数问题，我经历了重重挑战。

149
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:18,960
So therefore I think if you want to realize your dream, just work hard, believe in yourself.
因此，我认为如果你想实现梦想，就努力工作，相信自己。

150
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:27,960
So what do you want to do in the future or continue doing for the people here in last, or for the children?
那么，未来你想做什么，或者继续为这里的人们，特别是孩子们做些什么？

151
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,960
What do you want to continue to do?
你想继续做什么？

152
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:34,960
The main thing is you have to have a good brand, which is your name.
最重要的是你得有一个好品牌，也就是你的名字。

153
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:38,960
Whatever I say I should do in action, whatever I say be honest.
我说的每件事都要付诸行动，我说的每句话都要诚实。

154
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:44,960
In this way I can be a good example for my blind community and also for the society.
这样我就能成为盲人社区乃至整个社会的好榜样。

155
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,960
Can we add one more thing?
我们能再加一件事吗？

156
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,460
Yes.
可以。

157
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:55,960
I think the one more message thing I want to say is that so many people want to help for blind people.
我想说的另一条信息是，有太多人想帮助盲人。

158
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,960
They don't know how to help us.
他们不知道该怎么帮助我们。

159
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:02,960
I think we as a blind person, we should mingle in the society.
我认为作为盲人，我们应该融入社会。

160
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:07,960
I have so many sided friends, male friends, female friends.
我有各种各样的朋友，有男性朋友，也有女性朋友。

161
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:16,960
Even one of my female friends, her name is Tenzin Pema, she can guide me to the bathroom and she try to explain everything.
甚至我的一位女性朋友，她叫丹增佩玛，她能指引我去洗手间，并试图向我解释一切。

162
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:19,960
So this is I think very needed for blind people.
所以我认为这对盲人来说是非常必要的。

163
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:23,960
If we always stay by ourselves, I think this doesn't make sense.
如果我们总是独来独往，我觉得这没有意义。

164
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:29,960
We should mingle in the society, be friends with sided people, talk about cars or busker, whatever.
我们应该融入社会，与不同的人交朋友，聊聊汽车或街头艺人，什么都可以。

165
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:36,960
The second thing is that so many people think the blind path, the road for blind is not good.
第二件事是，很多人觉得盲道，也就是为盲人修的路，质量不好。

166
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:42,960
I think this is good, but the problem is not many blind people are on the blind path road.
我觉得这很好，但问题在于盲道上并没有多少盲人。

167
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:49,960
So what I am trying to say here for the blind community is that if we want to have a good road,
所以我想对盲人社区说的是，如果我们想要拥有一条好路，

168
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:56,960
we better to work with our white cane on this road, then people will recognize society cannot change us.
我们最好在这条路上使用我们的盲杖，这样人们就会意识到社会无法改变我们。

169
00:13:56,960 --> 00:14:05,960
But as a blind person, we have to change this society because the government, society, everybody is willing to help us.
但作为盲人，我们必须改变这个社会，因为政府、社会、每个人都愿意帮助我们。

170
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,960
The problem is they don't know how to help us.
问题在于他们不知道该如何帮助我们。

171
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:15,960
So this is what I am hoping to share with my fellow blind sisters and brothers. Thank you.
这就是我希望与我的盲人兄弟姐妹们分享的内容。谢谢。

172
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,960
Do you want to take live in your own hands? Yes.
你想把生活掌握在自己手中吗？是的。

173
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:21,960
You are in control? Correct. Great.
你在掌控之中？没错。太棒了。

174
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:26,960
I am nodding and I am smiling. I am so happy that we did this conversation. Yes, yes, yes.
我在点头，我在微笑。我很高兴我们进行了这次对话。是的，是的，是的。

175
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:32,960
Thank you so much. Do you want to shake hands? I am reaching out my hand. Thank you.
非常感谢。你想握手吗？我伸出手了。谢谢。

176
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,460
Thank you.
谢谢。

177
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:46,960
To translate from English, Chinese or Tibetan to Tibetan Braille,
要将英语、汉语或藏语翻译成藏文盲文，

178
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:53,960
Nima Pingtok is the founder of a groundbreaking Tibetan Braille translation software
尼玛平措是一款开创性的藏文盲文翻译软件的创始人，

179
